  - data governance
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  A benchmark and harness for evaluating data quality validation rules authored
  by large language models. Measures rule-level failure modes against a
  pre-specified taxonomy, retention on held-out data, stability across repeated
  generation, downstream model discrimination, subgroup composition shift, and
  authoring cost. Includes the corpus of 7,609 generated rules with failure
  codes and complete raw model responses.
